;; sealed-opaque graduation compatibility promise (2026-08-17): `sealed-opaque`
;; graduated, so its EXPERIMENTS[] row is gone -- but a downstream `build.tur`,
;; `~/.config/turmeric/experiments.tur`, or CLI invocation that still names it
;; must keep compiling.  `GRADUATED[]` in src/runtime/experiments.c is what
;; makes `--enable=sealed-opaque` a TUR-W0063 no-op instead of the hard
;; TUR-E0310 an unknown experiment name gets.
;;
;; Without this fixture graduation is a breaking change for exactly the people
;; who adopted the feature deliberately, which is the wrong population to
;; break.  The flag is in `flags`; the warning is asserted on stderr and the
;; program still runs, with enforcement on (it is unconditional now).
;;
;; This fixture WAS `sealed-opaque-gate-off`, which pinned the opposite promise
;; -- that `:sealed` parses and imposes nothing without the flag.  That promise
;; existed so adopting `:sealed` in a spice would not break consumers who had
;; not opted in; graduation is what retires it, so the fixture is repurposed
;; rather than deleted.  The casts below are unchanged and still in the
;; declaring module, where `::` is legal either way -- what moved is only which
;; claim the fixture makes about the flag.
(defopaque Tok :int :sealed)

(defn tok-new [n : int] : Tok (:: n Tok))
(defn tok-num [t : Tok] : int (:: t :int))

(defn main [] : int
  (println (tok-num (tok-new 42)))
  0)
